# React Native's Android build cannot use pnpm's symlinked node_modules.
#
# expo-modules-core compiles C++ through CMake + ninja. With the default (symlinked) layout,
# CMake resolves the same source through both its symlinked and its real `.pnpm/...` path, decides
# the generated manifest is stale, regenerates, and repeats — the build dies on
# `ninja: error: manifest 'build.ninja' still dirty after 100 tries`. It is not a path-length
# problem: Windows long paths are already enabled on this machine (LongPathsEnabled=1), and the
# CMAKE_OBJECT_PATH_MAX warnings that appear alongside it are a symptom of the same duplicated
# prefix, not the cause.
#
# The trade this makes: a hoisted tree is npm-shaped, so a package can import something it does
# not declare (a "phantom dependency") and pnpm will no longer catch it. That is a real loss of
# strictness, accepted because the alternative is that no Android build works at all — which
# would block every mobile track in the roadmap. See docs/DECISIONS.md D21.
node-linker=hoisted
